elon musk is known to have beef with a  lot of people he says he's not the  biggest fan of warren buffett he's  blasted mark zuckerberg's meta andy  frequently pokes fun at jeff bezos jeff  who  [Laughter]  but one guy he really really really  doesn't like is martin eberhard one of  tesla's co-founders he's the worst  person i have ever worked with and that  is saying something okay i've worked  with some real [ __ ] the two have  squabbled over who actually founded  tesla i'm not sure why he has to also  say that he was a founder when he wasn't  i don't understand that oh yeah whatever  it'd be accurate to say that there were  like five co-founders of tesla and he  counts himself as one of them martin  eberhard and fellow engineer mark  tarpening incorporated tesla motors in  2003. ian wright jb strabal and elon  musk join later however musk believes  there's no way tesla would have even  gone into production without him and jb  straubel its chief technology officer  musk pushed eberhard out of his role as  ceo and eventually out of the company in  2007 by then musk had been with tesla  for three years he used his earnings  from paypal to sign on as one of the  first investors in tesla in 2004 and  became chairman of the board  so why does elon musk despise martin  eberhard he even went so far as to say i  wish i had never met him  he believes eberhard nearly drove the  company into the ground when trying to  produce tesla's first car the roadster  you can have a car that's quick and you  can have a car it's electric but having  one that's both is how you make electric  cars popular trouble is musk didn't  think eberhard was capable of building  an electric sports car he says eberhard  wanted to outsource car battery  production to a barbecue manufacturing  factory in thailand as they were having  trouble finding a factory willing to  produce an advanced lithium-ion battery  pack when a tesla team went over to  check out the factory instead of a  factory they found a concrete slab with  posts holding up a roof as ashley vance  detailed in his book about elon musk  since the thai company couldn't make a  battery pack it caused issues for the  rest of the supply chain the plan was to  have the battery cells made in japan  shipped to thailand where they were  turned into a battery pack then shipped  to england where a company called lotus  engineering would build the body of the  car and attach the battery pack before  making its way to the initial market in  california musk alleges eberhard screwed  up in other areas too he says he  outsourced the carbon fiber body panels  to a company that couldn't make them  carbon fiber is a special material it's  very strong for it's very lightweight he  said the gaps between the body panels  were so big you could put your thumb in  between them unfortunately i don't have  pictures of the original roadster's body  panel issues but here are photos someone  posted on twitter of a model 3 with  large gaps between the panels  possibly the greatest mistake tesla made  in the early days was deciding on the  transmission system for the roadster  musk says eberhard refused to change the  motor size so to achieve 0 to 60 as  quickly as possible without a bigger  motor they required a 2-speed  transmission rather than a single speed  one the first gear would take the car  from 0-60 in less than 4 seconds the  second gear would take the car up to 130  miles an hour however the transmission  couldn't handle the jump from the first  gear to the second eberhard had vowed to  begin shipping the roadster in late 2007  but there was no way that could happen  with the transmission issues actually  the original plan was to deliver the car  in 2006. in the end production for the  roadster didn't begin until the fall of  2008. eberhard has responded to musk's  criticism in a message to me he wrote  that is of course ridiculous sure we  were over budget and behind schedule  which successful startup companies were  not  he went on to say since i left tesla 14  years ago which of tesla's cars has been  on schedule or on budget how is that  cyber truck going in reference to  tesla's futuristic truck musket said it  would make it to market by the end of  2021 but has now been delayed until 2023  musk also accuses eberhard of  intentionally deceiving him about the  true cost of the roadster when one of  tesla's investors sent its managing  director to do an audit they found that  the cost of producing the sports car  would be a hundred twenty thousand well  above the selling price of ninety two  thousand eberhart had said it would cost  65 000 to make tesla had already taken  deposits from hundreds of customers  promising the car would cost less than a  hundred thousand enough was enough and  as the roadster was way over budget and  late musk got on the phone with eberhard  and told him the board had decided he'd  be replaced as ceo demoting him to the  role of president of technology in  mid-2007 while keeping the same 200 000  salary he made as ceo eberhard was  pissed off and by the year's end he had  left the company all together i was  voted off the island and in in a rather  rude way tesla named michael marks as  interim ceo followed by permanent ceo  zev jarrory a silicon valley  semiconductor veteran before musk took  over the top job in the fall of 2008.  musk may have blamed eberhard for  tesla's troubles however eberhard has  blamed musk for the roadster's problems  in this newsweek article from 2008  eberhard accused musk of interfering  with the design of the car demanding  changes that were costly and led to  delays these included installing  electronic door latches building a  lightweight carbon fiber body and  lowering the door sill by two inches  musk denied that those changes were the  cause of the delays in told fortune  magazine he was quote too busy trying to  fix the bleeping mess he as an eberhard  left in 2009 eberhard sued musk alleging  musk began a pattern of defaming and  disparaging him in the media the lawsuit  also states musk set out to rewrite  history by falsely claiming that he was  the founder or creator of tesla motors  when someone on twitter pointed out musk  was not the founder musk argued founding  means more than filing papers to start a  company he says without him tesla motors  had no employees no ip address no  designs no prototype literally nothing  but a business plan  in its counter claim against eberhard  tesla and musk dismissed eberhard's  lawsuit as quote nothing more than to  curb open discourse on matters of  importance to the public and to extract  money from tesla in the end they agreed  to a settlement elon musk jb strabal and  ian wright were allowed to call  themselves co-founders alongside mark  tarpening and martin eberhard by the way  eberhard mentioned in his lawsuit that  he didn't receive the second roadster  tesla ever produced as promised which  musk sold to a friend the one he did  finally get had been smashed into the  back of a truck by an employee during an  endurance test almost completely  totaling the vehicle it was a wreck  perhaps a metaphor for the relationship  between musk and eberhard  after leaving tesla everhard briefly led  volkswagen's evie development in the us  was the vp of ativa which is now lucid  motors for only six weeks and also ran  his own electric startup now he's  enjoying retirement while enjoying it as  much as he can except when musk brings  up his name i just buy his money heart  eberhard ended his message to me by  saying i find it strange that musk feels  he must still spend his energy  criticizing me when my startup company  with all its flaws has revolutionized  the entire automotive industry and has  made musk the richest man in the world  i'd like to take the opportunity to  thank the sponsor of this video  magnesium breakthrough by by optimizers  i used to have a lot of trouble sleeping  but ever since i've been taking  magnesium bre